/-!
# The degree-90 polynomial of the 16-circle optimum

`H16coeffs` lists the 91 integer coefficients of `H16`, from the constant term up to `q^90`.  The optimum
`q16 = cos θ` (`θ` the angular step between consecutive boundary circles) is the largest real root of
`H16`, and `R16 = 1 + √(2 / (1 - q16))` (see `Exact16.lean`).  The polynomial was found by exact symbolic
elimination outside Lean; every property used is verified in Lean (`Tower16.lean`, `Root16.lean`).
-/

